---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { offer } from "../lib/offer";

const linkClass =
  "link";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Sale · Gerfaut Premium"
  description="The terms of sale of Gerfaut Premium: seller, plans and prices, your Premium key, payment in bitcoin, no refund, data, liability and applicable law."
>
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="site-container">
      <article class="mx-auto max-w-[68ch]">
        <h1
          class="font-display text-[2rem] leading-[1.1] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] sm:text-[2.5rem]"
        >
          Terms of Sale
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">
          Gerfaut Premium &middot; Last updated
          <time datetime="2026-09-21">21 September 2026</time>
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-12 border-t border-border pt-6 text-h2 font-display">1. Seller</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Gerfaut Premium is sold by Monsieur Loïc Morel, sole trader
          (entreprise individuelle) registered in France under SIRET
          850&nbsp;401&nbsp;290&nbsp;00034 and trading as Pandul. Address: 61
          rue de Lyon, 75012 Paris, France. Contact:
          <a href="mailto:info@pandul.fr" class={linkClass}>info@pandul.fr</a>.
          VAT is not applicable under article 293 B of the French General Tax
          Code (CGI).
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 border-t border-border pt-6 text-h2 font-display">2. What you buy</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Prepaid time on the Gerfaut alert service, tied to a Premium key.
          From our server, the service watches the Bitcoin wallets you
          register and notifies you through the channels you choose (ntfy,
          Telegram, e-mail, webhook), plus the other Premium services listed
          on the Premium page as they become available. A webhook must point
          at a host the internet can reach: the server refuses a private or
          local address. It is a monitoring service: it never holds keys or
          funds and cannot move them.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 border-t border-border pt-6 text-h2 font-display">3. Plans and prices</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          1 month: 5&nbsp;€. 6 months: 24&nbsp;€. 1 year: 36&nbsp;€.
          {offer.active && (
            <>
              {" "}Launch offer: 1 year for {offer.price}&nbsp;€ instead of
              {offer.standard}&nbsp;€ for every purchase made until
              {offer.until} inclusive (UTC); from the next day the standard
              price applies.
            </>
          )}
          {" "}Prices are in euro and paid in bitcoin at the rate shown at
          checkout. Paid time adds to the end of the time you already have.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 border-t border-border pt-6 text-h2 font-display">4. Your Premium key</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          The Premium key is shown once, at checkout, before you pay. It is
          the only way to use the time you bought. We store only a hash of it
          and cannot recover, reset or re-issue a lost key. Anyone holding the
          key can use the account. Keep it like a password.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 border-t border-border pt-6 text-h2 font-display">5. Payment</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Payments go through our own Bark Pay instance and settle on Bitcoin
          (Ark, Lightning or on-chain). Time is credited when the payment is
          confirmed. An underpaid charge is not credited until it is topped
          up; the checkout page shows the remaining amount. An overpayment is
          treated as paid and the difference is not refunded.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 border-t border-border pt-6 text-h2 font-display">6. No refund</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Premium is a prepaid service that starts the moment your payment is
          confirmed. By paying, you expressly agree that the service begins at
          once and you waive your right of withdrawal. Payment is final and
          not refundable, except as stated in section 9.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 border-t border-border pt-6 text-h2 font-display">
          7. What the service can and cannot do
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Alerts are sent as fast as the Bitcoin network and our servers
          allow, usually within seconds. We do not guarantee delivery time or
          availability; incidents are published on
          <a href="https://status.gerfaut-wallet.com" class={linkClass}
            >status.gerfaut-wallet.com</a
          >. The service does not prevent theft and cannot guarantee that
          every movement is detected: network, channel or server outages
          happen. Use it as one layer among others. Nothing here is financial
          advice.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 border-t border-border pt-6 text-h2 font-display">8. Your data</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          We store the descriptors you register, the addresses derived from
          them, the coins and movements seen on them, the channels you add,
          and the hash of your Premium key. A Telegram channel also holds the name
          Telegram gives the chat, a first name or a group title, so you can
          see where the alerts land; an e-mail address you have not confirmed
          waits beside its channel until you type its code back. We store no
          other name, no e-mail unless you add one as a channel, no IP address
          and no request logs. Stopping the watch on a wallet, or removing a
          watched wallet from the app, deletes its data on the server. One
          exception: a wallet refused for holding more than 5,000 unspent
          coins leaves, for one hour, a hash of its descriptor and your
          account, made with a secret of the server and never the descriptor
          itself, so that sending it again is refused without a new scan; that
          hash is deleted within the following hour, and at once with your
          account. The server deletes everything it holds under a key 90 days after the
          paid time on that key runs out; a key that was never paid for is
          deleted 30 days after it was created. To delete everything now, use
          "Forget this key" in the app, which offers to delete your data on
          the server as well, or write to
          <a href="mailto:info@pandul.fr" class={linkClass}>info@pandul.fr</a>
          with your Premium key. We operate the servers ourselves, in Canada and
          France. The data controller is Loïc Morel.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 border-t border-border pt-6 text-h2 font-display">
          9. Changes and discontinuation
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          We may change or discontinue a service with 30 days' notice on the
          status page. If we discontinue the alert service, unused time is
          refunded pro rata in bitcoin on request.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 border-t border-border pt-6 text-h2 font-display">10. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Do not register wallets you have no right to monitor. One key
          watches up to 21 wallets and 10 channels and may send 60 requests
          per minute; requests are also limited per network address on every
          route. The server refuses what goes past either limit with a clear
          error. A wallet that holds more than 5,000 unspent coins is refused:
          the server stops watching it and says why. Sent again by the same
          key within the hour, it gets the same refusal without a new scan.
          Wallets added or changed
          are limited to 30 an hour per key; a rename does not count. Messages
          sent on the spot, a channel test or the confirmation
          e-mail of a new address, are limited to five an hour per account.
          E-mail alerts are limited to 20 per account per UTC day, within the
          budget the server holds with its mail provider; past either, e-mail
          alerts are sent the next day rather than dropped, and the other
          channels are unaffected. We may stop serving a key that abuses the
          service.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 border-t border-border pt-6 text-h2 font-display">11. Liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          To the extent the law allows, our liability is limited to the
          amount you paid in the 12 months before the claim. Nothing here
          excludes liability that cannot be excluded under French consumer
          law.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 border-t border-border pt-6 text-h2 font-display">12. Law and complaints</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          French law applies. For any complaint, write to
          <a href="mailto:info@pandul.fr" class={linkClass}>info@pandul.fr</a>
          with your Premium key.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 border-t border-border pt-6 text-h2 font-display">13. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Changes are posted on this page with their date. The terms in force
          when you paid apply to that purchase.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
